From 585d31f56f685c7180a00e94d80d1826e312a65e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 22:19:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 661/689] ozone/aros: F11 fullscreen, Alt+F11 on an own screen,
 Latin-1 titles
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fullscreen resized the framed window to the Workbench work area, the same
as Maximize. It now reopens the Intuition window, since Intuition cannot
change a window's border or screen in place:

- F11: a borderless window filling the whole Workbench screen.
- Alt+F11: a screen of Chromium's own (like Workbench, draggable, with
  its title bar kept) holding a borderless backdrop window, so it can be
  dragged down or flipped away like any AROS screen. Alt+F11 while
  fullscreen on Workbench moves it to the own screen.

Menus and popups open on their parent's custom screen. The switch runs
as a posted task (it drains the IDCMP port, and F11 arrives inside that
port's dispatch), and window_ and the backing store are swapped under the
presentation lock the compositor draws under.

AROS's PC keyboard drivers report F11 as Amiga Help (i8042 stdkeytable),
so Help maps to F11.

Window and screen titles are converted to Latin-1, which Intuition draws:
page titles were passed as UTF-8, so "Leo’s" showed as "Leoâ..s".
Typographic quotes, dashes and ellipses become ASCII, anything else
outside Latin-1 '?'.
